{
    "id": 181,
    "title": "Buttons: one standard (brand brown, page-colour text), Claim that stands out, pop-ups dim the page, one search bar look",
    "why": "Jason, 2026-11-19: \"the button color should be our standard button color default. The Text color should match the bg color\"; \"popups should dim bg\"; \"claim needs to pop\"; \"maybe the header and hero should have a small cream separator?\"; \"go ahead, build it\". (1) Tokens --tv-btn #92400E, --tv-btn-text #E4DCC5 (5.18:1), --tv-btn-hover #78350F (his pick, B, 6.63:1), and the reverse for dark bars (--tv-btn-inv). 67 button rules in 40 files now use them; the Tailwind buttons that had ink on brown (2.6:1) are fixed. (2) Claim on a listing's photo: \"Claim this business\" in the standard button with the store icon and \"Add your own photos, hours and more\" under it. (3) The Peek card dims the page behind it; Open listing is its one filled button. (4) The message box on an unclaimed listing: Call them leads, Leave a message and Check a reply are outlined. (5) The home bar and Get Local's: field colour with its edge, sentence case (\"What are you looking for?\" in place of \"Discover more\", decisions/0138's note), a × to clear, the Go icon in the page colour. (6) A thin cream line under the header. Email templates are untouched. FAQ: the search's words box, Peek, claiming.",
